WEBVTT

1
00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
Begin with 1,000 observations. 200 object · 800 no object.
Each dot represents 10 cases. Object prevalence is 20%.

2
00:06.000 --> 00:12.000
Flag 80% of object cases. 160 true alerts · 40 missed.
Recall = P(alert | object) = 0.8. This is not alert correctness.

3
00:12.000 --> 00:18.000
Also flag 10% of non-objects. 80 false alerts · 720 unflagged.
True and false alerts both appear in the denominator of precision.

4
00:18.000 --> 00:24.000
Look only among the alerts. P(object | alert) = 160/240.
160 + 80 = 240 total alerts. Posterior probability is 2/3.
